    <briefdescription>
<para>South Korean calendars. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Public holidays: <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Saturdays </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Sundays </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>New Year&apos;s Day, January 1st </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Independence Day, March 1st </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Arbour Day, April 5th (until 2005) </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Labour Day, May 1st </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Children&apos;s Day, May 5th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Memorial Day, June 6th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Constitution Day, July 17th (until 2007) </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Liberation Day, August 15th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>National Fondation Day, October 3th </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Christmas Day, December 25th </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para><para>Other holidays for which no rule is given (data available for 2004-2012 only:) <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Lunar New Year, the last day of the previous lunar year, January 1st, 2nd in lunar calendar </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Election Days </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>National Assemblies </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Presidency </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Regional Election Days </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Buddha&apos;s birthday, April 8th in lunar calendar </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Harvest Moon Day, August 14th, 15th, 16th in lunar calendar </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para><para>Holidays for the Korea exchange (data from <ulink url="http://eng.krx.co.kr/m8/m8_6/m8_6_1/JHPENG08006_01.jsp">http://eng.krx.co.kr/m8/m8_6/m8_6_1/JHPENG08006_01.jsp</ulink> or <ulink url="http://www.dooriworld.com/daishin/holiday/holiday.html">http://www.dooriworld.com/daishin/holiday/holiday.html</ulink>): <itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para>Public holidays as listed above </para></listitem>
<listitem>
<para>Year-end closing </para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
